13123	{"artifactId":"HLD-6a1315585c38c41c","entry":{"id":"migrated-HLD-6a1315585c38c41c-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-08T18:56:24.018Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every S004 acceptance criterion has a designed home: ac1 (tasks with dependsOn/acceptanceChecks and Passed/Failed/Unrecorded/unplanned), ac2 (stage reason plus cited records), ac3 (conflict), ac4 (rejected vs pending, original verdict plus override), ac5 (two open paths) and ac6 (the review-without-build notice).","evidence":"sc6 ItemDetailsViewModel carries tasks[] (resultLabel, planned, dependsOn, acceptanceChecks), taskCounts {passed, failed, unrecorded, unplanned}, stageReason {text, artifactIds}, conflict, evidence[] (approvalLabel, reviewLabel, overrideLabel, opensIn) and notices[]. The daemon side backs each field: types.ts:198 TaskResult 'passed'|'failed'|'unrecorded'; :214 validation counts; :164 reason {text, artifactIds}; :189 review.override; :280 approval.state 'approved'|'rejected'|'pending'; :124 NoticeCode 'review-without-build'.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The HLD's additive change to the review pane does not build a DEF non-goal.","evidence":"DEF §3 still lists the non-goal 'Changing the existing VS Code document review pane … does not alter it' (DEF.md:68). Constraint k10 (DEF.md:94, amended by commit 62392461 from a 2026-10-09 stakeholder decision, c24) explicitly allows 'one additive entry point that opens a given artifact by id, read-only when it is not pending'. sc7 stays inside k10: it adds openArtifact and leaves open() and dispose() unchanged. The DEF's own non-goal text is now stale against k10, which is a wording issue in the DEF, not in the HLD.","action":"Optionally reword the DEF non-goal so it reads 'beyond the one k10 entry point', keeping the DEF and the HLD consistent.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared IPC client sets no timeout of its own, so the delivery client has to race a deadline.","evidence":"rpc() (ipc-client.ts:46-84) returns a Promise that settles only on a 'data' line or a socket 'error'. It has no setTimeout and no socket.setTimeout. createIpcClient (:115-120) passes rpc through unchanged. [files: src/shared/ipc-client.ts]","action":"none. When the deadline wins, the LLD should also say whether the dangling socket is left open or destroyed. rpc exposes no handle, so it is left open.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon returns delivery failures as a structured { error } result arm, and socket-level failures reject, so the client can tell 'daemon-unavailable' apart from 'read-failed'.","evidence":"handleDelivery and handleDeliveryEvidence never throw. They return { error: ... } as the result (handlers.ts:58, 83, 107, 109, 117, 124, 132, 135). rpc rejects with 'daemon is not running — start it with: insrc daemon start' on ENOENT/ECONNREFUSED (ipc-client.ts:77-78), and rejects with the raw error on any other socket error. [files: src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts, src/shared/ipc-client.ts]","action":"The LLD should name the rule that classifies a rejection: the 'daemon is not running' prefix maps to daemon-unavailable, and other socket errors map to read-failed or unavailable.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The review pane is created only when insrc.chat.enabled is on, so the board may have no pane to open.","evidence":"extension.ts:424-425 `const chatEnabled = ... get<boolean>('insrc.chat.enabled') === true; if (chatEnabled) {` and the docsReviewHost is created at :607 inside that block, with its command at :631. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"The board's wiring in extension.ts needs a nullable handle to docsReviewHost. Today it is a block-scoped const inside the if.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Reused shapes exist as stated: Envelope<T> {v:1, payload}, DocsReviewHost {open, dispose} with a deps-injected factory and ChatPanelLogger, and the delivery-contract mirror typing both methods without callers.","evidence":"protocol.ts:38-40 `export interface Envelope<T> { readonly v: 1; readonly payload: T;`; docs-review-panel.ts:39-42 `export interface DocsReviewHost { open(): void; dispose(): void; }`, :30-37 DocsReviewHostDeps with `logger?: ChatPanelLogger`, :45 NOOP_LOGGER {warn, error}; delivery-contract.ts:39-42 DeliveryMethods for both methods. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The six enum types sc4 imports (DeliveryStage, AttentionReason, NoticeCode, TaskResult, ApprovalState, ReviewVerdict) are not yet in the mirror, so they must be added. They are exported from src/workflow/delivery/types.ts.","evidence":"The mirror re-exports only DeliveryError…DeliverySnapshotResponse (delivery-contract.ts:26-36). types.ts exports ReviewVerdict (:17, a re-export from review/types), ApprovalState (:25), NoticeCode (:117), DeliveryStage (:148), TaskResult (:198) and AttentionReason (:208). tsconfig.delivery-contract.json compiles src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts, src/workflow/delivery/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"sc7's openArtifact({artifactId, mdPath}) can be served by the pane's existing read path, because the pane reads content by mdPath and the delivery entry supplies an mdPath that resolves the same way.","evidence":"The client resolves id->mdPath from a map that only pending() fills (docs-review-client.ts:74-77, 88), then calls workflow.artifactContent {mdPath} (:97-100). For a non-pending artifact the id is not in that map, so passing mdPath explicitly is required, as sc7 does. The delivery mdPath comes from the same resolveDocsMarkdown/deriveMdPath (markdown.ts:99-110) that handleArtifactContent uses (artifact-content.ts:155). It is non-null whenever openWith is 'review-view' (snapshot.ts:102-103). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-client.ts, src/workflow/artifact-content.ts, src/workflow/delivery/markdown.ts]","action":"none. Note for s4: the pane's client sends no `repo`, so content() falls back to the daemon's INSRC_REPO, while the board sends the workspace root. The LLD should state that this mismatch is accepted or handled.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The board host takes the plugin's ChatPanelLogger and logs through error() and warn(), wired from extension.ts.","evidence":"ChatPanelLogger has warn and error (docs-review-panel.ts:45 NOOP_LOGGER). The only shared logger instance in extension.ts is `const panelLog = { warn: ... }` (extension.ts:255), which has no error(). The docsReviewHost is created without a logger (:607-630). I did not open ChatPanelLogger's declaration to see whether error is optional, so I could not confirm that extension.ts can hand the board a ChatPanelLogger without a new adapter. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"s1's LLD should name the logger instance the board host receives in extension.ts. If ChatPanelLogger.error is required, it should add an error sink.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The PLAN-join rule works on stored records: a snapshot task item's sourceIds contain the PLAN task id ('t1'…), and PlanTask carries id, dependsOn and acceptanceChecks.","evidence":"graph.ts addTasks (:371-416) reads body.tasks[].id from PLAN/BUILD records, keeps only ids of the t<n> form, and builds the task item with `sourceIds: [taskId]` (:411), adding to it when the same id repeats (:401). plan.ts:63-70 PlanTask has `id` ('t1','t2'...), `dependsOn: readonly string[]` and `acceptanceChecks: readonly string[]`. deliveryEvidence returns `body: record.body` unchanged (handlers.ts:142), so the board reads the same body.tasks. [files: src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/plan.ts]","action":"none. The defensive read stated in the risk table covers older PLANs that lack these fields.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The board handles snapshot versioning (schemaVersion 1) and the DEF's additive-only evolution of the delivery contract.","evidence":"DeliverySnapshot.schemaVersion is the literal 1 (types.ts:311). The HLD never states what the client does if a response carries a different schemaVersion, or whether unknown additive fields are ignored. The type-level mirror pins compile-time drift (delivery-contract.ts:9-11), but runtime handling is not described anywhere in the HLD.","action":"sc1 should state the runtime check: reject a schemaVersion other than 1 as 'read-failed' with a clear message, and ignore unknown fields.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The HLD leaves E1's daemon contract (sc7) unchanged and consumes it as published; the PLAN detail is read through the existing workflow.deliveryEvidence without any daemon change.","evidence":"handleDeliveryEvidence accepts any artifact id that matches `^(SPEC|DEF|HLD|LLD|PLAN|BUILD|...)-[0-9a-f]{16}(-…)?$` (handlers.ts:42, 109), not only evidence-read records. It returns meta, body and renderedMarkdown for any store record (:138-144), so a PLAN can be read with no daemon change. index.ts:719-724 registers it. [files: src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each failure has a detectable signal and a stated handling: no workspace, daemon down, {error} arm, timeout, superseded response, PLAN read failure, pane unavailable.","evidence":"sc1 sends 'no-workspace' without calling the daemon. Socket failures and the {error} result arm (handlers.ts never throw) map to DeliveryFailureKind. Timeouts come from a deadline race, because rpc has none (ipc-client.ts:46-84). sc2 maps unavailable/no-workspace to 'unavailable' and read-failed/timed-out to 'failed', each keeping `last`. requestSeq drops stale responses. sc6.planNotice covers a failed PLAN read. When the pane is absent, the record falls back to the read-only deliveryEvidence path (risk table plus s4 boundary text).","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Acceptance criteria map to named tests that can run under the plugin's existing suite, including s1 ac4 (out-of-order fakes), s1 ac6 (temporary git repo), s4 ac5 (both open paths with the pane's tests unchanged) and s5 ac5 (measured fixture).","evidence":"vscode-plugin/package.json:770 `\"test\": \"tsx --test 'src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts'\"`. The host and client are deps-injected and vscode-free (the rpc and repo deps in sc1), so fakes can drive ac4. The HLD's §6 story boundaries name the ac4, ac6 and ac5 tests explicitly and require every AC to map to a named LLD test. ac6 can call the read-only handlers (handlers.ts, 'neither writes') against a temp repo. [files: vscode-plugin/package.json]","action":"none. s1's LLD should say whether ac6 calls handleDelivery directly or goes through a live daemon.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-08T18:56:24.018Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
